<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guatemala City</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1776</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Nueva Guatemala de la Asunción</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a> City was founded in 1776 as the new capital of the Captaincy General of Guatemala, after earthquakes ruined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a>, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigua-guatemala">Antigua Guatemala</a>. It grew over the site of the ancient Maya city of Kaminaljuyu. It was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-republic-of-central-america">Federal Republic of Central America</a> until 1834 and has since been the capital of Guatemala.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guatemala-city.jpg" alt="Guatemala City" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rene Hernandez · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ciudad_de_Guatemala,_CA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
